{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfe2FaaczKuw6pVWYxdiE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted an equal-weight portfolio of the 5/21-day moving-average crossover signal across all 47 hedged industries. Its training Sharpe is 0.10. It was the only signal family with a positive return in every third of 1970–1999, but its one validation check came back **FAIL**.\n\nThe training data shows almost no persistent edge: how individual signals rank in the first half of 1970–1999 has essentially zero correlation with how they rank in the second half. I used just 1 of the 200 backtest calls and stopped there on purpose. Testing many portfolios until one happened to PASS would mostly pick up noise from the 2000–2012 holdout. That would inflate the reported validation Sharpe without giving a strategy likely to work on new data. So the submitted portfolio is the one I chose from training data alone, and its validation Sharpe is probably modest."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":576,"cache_read_input_tokens":9667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":576},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c5a67ce-1c4f-4853-abc8-db4c470b4132","uuid":"8d3dd13a-c2cd-46b4-a48b-5fd8287728eb","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:13:52.946Z","request_id":"req_011Cfe2FaKyihvGcecjNxDFR"}
